{# How to name a collection in a call. The refused calls give a dataset name, a changed name
   or a collection that the chat cannot read. #}
Naming a collection

1. Leave out collectionname to search every collection of this chat. That is correct for most questions.
2. When you must give a collection, copy its name exactly from {{ tool('list_collections') }}, or from the collectionname of a result row.
3. A dataset is not a collection. The dataset tables/ehudx is in the collection tables. Give tables.
4. Do not change a name. Do not add a space, change a capital letter or translate it.
5. When a call says that a collection is outside the permitted collections, this chat cannot read it. Do not send the call again. Use the collections of this chat.

To read a document, give the collectionname of the same result row as its file_hash.
